course: dictionary
lesson: 6518
title: The New Stone Age
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are long, but their parts can help. Neolithic is about the Stone Age, and «neo» in it means new, so the Neolithic is the New Stone Age.
explain: Read the clue in the sentence: «It was Mummy and the other Neolithic ladies.» The word Neolithic tells us which ladies, so it describes people from a long time ago. Swap in a word that means the same kind of thing, like «ancient»: «the other ancient ladies». It still makes sense, so you have the right idea.
explain: The dictionary gives the full meaning: belonging to the New Stone Age, when people began farming, keeping animals, making pottery and polished stone tools, and living in villages. Check it against the sentence, and then you know you are right.
fact: Neolithic means belonging to the New Stone Age, the last part of the Stone Age.
fact: In Britain, the Neolithic was about 4000 to 2500 BC.
fact: In the Neolithic, people began farming, keeping animals, making pottery and polished stone tools, and living in villages.
fact: Stonehenge's first stages and Skara Brae in Orkney were built in the Neolithic.
fact: Kipling calls Taffy and her father «Neolithic» people, but the invention of writing in his story is made up: real writing began in Mesopotamia and Egypt around 3200 BC.
exercise: «I had to pay two deerskins, soft ones with fringes, to the Stranger-man.» What did Tegumai pay? | *Two deerskins | Two stone tools | Two villages | Two clay pots
exercise: Which place was built in the Neolithic? | Hadrian's Wall | The Tower of London | *Skara Brae in Orkney | The Pyramids of Giza
exercise: Which of these did people begin doing in the Neolithic? | *Farming and keeping animals | Writing on computers | Flying in aeroplanes | Building railways
test: Which description fits the Neolithic best? | The Iron Age, when people used iron for weapons | *The New Stone Age, when people farmed and lived in villages | The time of the Roman Empire in Britain | The age of the first computers
test: In Kipling's Just So Stories, what is made up about Taffy's people? | *They invent writing | They make pottery | They live by a river | They keep animals
exam: Which word means the New Stone Age, when people began farming in Britain around 4000 to 2500 BC? | Roman | Medieval | *Neolithic | Victorian
